            <ArticleTitle>Aneurysm of Vieussens' arterial ring in a patient studied with coronary computed tomography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S84-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2459/JCM.0b013e328359dd44</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of Vieussens' arterial ring aneurysm in a patient who underwent coronary computed tomography. Vieussens' arterial ring is a remnant of the embryonic conotruncal circle. Only four cases of aneurysm are described in literature. This is the first reported case in which a dilated Vieussens' arterial ring is observed without coronary stenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
